{"id":"0c6d990a-a8cc-4fb4-a1dc-8a850c56b9e5","object":"chat.completion","created":1793243428,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"thought\":\"I now have pages 51-52 covering Table 4 (Training Data, Hallucination, Agent Behavior, Self reflection, Safety) and the conclusion stating all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification. I'll write the outlook note from this evidence, then compose the report using all five notes.\",\"code\":\"note = write_note(title=\\\"outlook\\\", content=\\\"Outlook: Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics: Training Data, Hallucination, Agent Behavior, Self reflection, Safety. Training Data needs inference-time reasoning data, stable RL, and VLA/multimodal signals; hallucination calls for self-verification and mechanistic interpretability; agent behavior needs scalable simulation and role playing; self reflection needs in-model metareasoning and metacognition; safety covers responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, and standardized benchmarks like AgentHarm. Conclusion (p.52) states the taxonomy's three categories (reasoning, acting via tools/robotics, interacting socially) complement each other, with reasoning as the base; robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification. Acting and interacting also generate training data for further pretraining/finetuning. References begin at end of p.52.\\\", evidence_ids=[\\\"ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9\\\", \\\"ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3\\\"], section=\\\"outlook\\\")\\nprint(note)\"}"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8177,"completion_tokens":326,"total_tokens":8503,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5632},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":5632,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":2545},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}